  "protocol": "RE-RANKING over RELISH labelled candidate lists, identical to relish-restricted/2. Only the scoring function differs: MedCPT article-encoder cosine, against our own embedding cosine (like-for-like) and against our deployed ranker (what a searcher receives).",
  "encoder_choice": "Both sides of every pair go through MedCPT's ARTICLE encoder, because RELISH is article-to-article similarity. Using the query encoder on the seed was rejected: it truncates at 64 tokens and a seed is a whole abstract, so it would have measured truncation. Article-against-article is correct for the task but is not a configuration MedCPT was trained on, which is a limitation of this comparison rather than a property of the model.",
