  "disclosures": [
    "This is a genuine head-to-head on identical data, unlike the LitSense column of Table 9, which is quoted from their paper on a split they do not publish. The LitSense figures are carried here only so the three can be seen together, and they remain not comparable cell for cell.",
    "MedCPT is measured here as a similarity function over a fixed labelled list, which is what this task requires. It says nothing about what MedCPT would retrieve from its own index over all of PubMed, and nothing about its cross-encoder, which is not part of this drop.",
    "Candidate list lengths are asserted equal to the ones our own run scored, for every seed, before anything is computed. A missing embedding would have shortened a list, and a shorter list is an easier list, so the failure would have looked like MedCPT winning.",
    "The comparison to quote for a claim about EMBEDDINGS is against ours_similarity_only. The comparison against ours_deployed_ranker includes our citation and recency priors and is the comparison for a claim about the deployed service."
